      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I regularly see stream snipers as well. They send friend requests to streamers from a different room so you can't stop them from sending more requests.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-24T06:41:59.536Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, you can search for a player, regardless if they are in your room, and friend or mute them. Blocking them from another room does not work. This should be just as important as adding friends, as some people leave the room before you are given a chance to block them.\n\nI came across two players that would greet people walking near them with profanity and insults. I did not block them at the time because I had just launched the menu to leave the room. I remembered their names, but was unable to block them from another room. The next day, I joined a random room and they happened to be there. They were still harassing people. I would have rather already had them blocked than have to navigate the menu with two people in my face shouting profanity and insults.",
